/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." 13194139535338 true] [17592186344465 1113 #uuid "04522178-100e-570d-8bab-ad0415e9727a" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344465 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344467 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344468 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344469 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344470 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344471 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1041 "selection" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344471 13194139535338 true] [17592186344466 1110 #uuid "2b8c0afa-2f73-51dd-b12f-075a7560de71" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344467 1034 "\\frac{4}{y}" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535338 true] [17592186344467 1111 #uuid "4a33399f-b4d5-5f6b-91dc-15f5d9c56441" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344468 1034 "\\frac{2}{y}" 13194139535338 true] [17592186344468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535338 true] [175